# The foundation is a submodule. It is formatted in the repository it belongs
# to, with the same rules.
upstream/

# The documentation is laid out by hand. Prettier would realign tables and
# rewrap paragraphs, which would hide every change of content behind
# formatting noise.
*.md

# The same goes for the workflows and templates: they hold check scripts in
# block scalars, and rewriting the scaffolding around them brings nothing but
# unreadable diffs at exactly the places that have to be readable.
.github/

# drizzle-kit generates the migrations and rewrites the meta folder on every
# run. Formatting it only gets it back reformatted at the next generate, and a
# migration that has run is not changed, not even in its whitespace.
packages/server/migrations/

# A version of an entry in a package is not changed once it is merged, not
# even in its whitespace (ADR 0005, point 7). A newer Prettier that lays out
# JSON differently would otherwise demand exactly the change the comparison
# with main refuses.
pakete/
